          "findings": [
            "The seven UI bindings are represented by the three intended variants; the shared tier values, five-effective-stack cap, 2.5-second expiry, first qualifying weakspot hit, first-target body-hit reset, and weapon-switch behavior are consistent with the verified implementation.",
            "Force Sword M1/M2 sticky weakspot ticks and M3's lack of sticky settings are described distinctly.",
            "The Dual Shivs text correctly distinguishes thrown knives from melee proc/reset events and says they inherit the bonus available when the throw action starts."
          ]
        },
        "examples_and_math": {
          "accepted": true,
          "findings": [
            "Tier IV at five stacks is +30%; the 300 to 390 example is explicitly a post-power-type-curve power input before Executor, not final HP damage.",
            "The existing +20% example adds the two same-stage bonuses to 1.50 and correctly describes the relative increase as 25%.",
            "The Dual Shivs example uses three existing stacks (+18%) and 300 × 1.18 = 354 as a power input; the stated caveat avoids presenting it as final damage.",
            "The multi-target example only promises the stacks for subsequent attacks after qualifying proc events are processed; it does not claim the current hit is retroactively recalculated."
          ]
        },
        "projectile_snapshot_timing": {
          "accepted": true,
          "findings": [
            "ActionSpawnProjectile.start generates the projectile before the configured 0.2-second fire time. The item_projectile template copies the owner stat-buff table at projectile creation, and PlayerProjectileUnitBuffExtension retains that copy without updating it.",
            "ProjectileDamageExtension sends the projectile's ranged attack through Attack; Attack reads the projectile extension's copied stat buffs, and PowerLevel consumes generic power_level_modifier. Existing Executor stacks present in the start-time snapshot therefore benefit the thrown knife.",
            "Switching weapons or expiring the owner's Executor stacks after projectile generation does not modify the existing projectile snapshot. A ranged thrown hit does not add, clear, or refresh Executor stacks."
          ]
        },
        "variants_bindings_localization": {
