      "scope": "Reviewed special-attack event behavior and whether Dual Shivs thrown projectiles inherit active Executor Power. The integrated executor-config.json has not yet received this peer review.",
      "verified": [
        "Combatknife P1 M1/M2 special actions use sweep with the jab_special damage profile. The profile marks weapon_special but has no skip_on_hit_proc; ActionSweep submits melee Attack.execute hits, so an actual weakspot hit can satisfy Executor's melee-and-weakspot gate.",
        "Force Sword P1 M1/M2 sticky attacks execute three damage instances per sticky profile tick. ActionSweep submits each tick as melee against target_index 1 and computes its weakspot result; each qualifying weakspot tick can add a stack, while a body hit on that first target can clear active stacks. Force Sword P1 M3 has no sticky settings. The shared Executor gate does not exclude weapon_special.",
        "Dual Shivs P1 M1/M2 special throw uses ActionWeaponThrow, which inherits ActionSpawnProjectile. Its projectile hit is attack_type ranged, so it cannot add or clear Executor stacks, whose parent gate is melee-only.",
        "Dual Shivs thrown damage can benefit from active generic power_level_modifier stacks if those stacks are present in the player's stat-buff snapshot when the projectile is spawned. item_projectile_unit_template shallow-copies owner stat_buffs into PlayerProjectileUnitBuffExtension; Attack later reads stat_buffs from the projectile extension, and PowerLevel consumes the generic power_level_modifier. This is a spawn-time snapshot: switching weapons or the owner's later buff expiry does not update an already spawned projectile's copied table."
      ],
